01:13:56,129 --> 01:14:02,129
Gandhi is a 1982 biographical film directed and produced by
Richard Attenborough and written by John Briley.

13
01:20:05,806 --> 01:20:11,806
It is based on the life of Mahatma Gandhi (portrayed by Ben Kingsley), a major leader in the
Indian independence movement against the British Empire during the 20th century.

14
01:26:15,483 --> 01:26:21,483
It covers Gandhi's life from a defining moment in 1893, as he is thrown off a South African train for
being in a whites-only compartment and concludes with his assassination and funeral in 1948.

15
01:32:25,161 --> 01:32:31,161
Although a practising Hindu, Gandhi's embracing of other faiths,
particularly Christianity and Islam, is also depicted.

16
01:38:34,838 --> 01:38:40,838
Over 300,000 extras appeared in the film, believed
to be the most in any film made.

17
01:44:44,516 --> 01:44:50,516
Gandhi was released by Columbia Pictures in India on 30 November 1982, in the
United Kingdom on 3 December, and in the United States on 8 December.

18
01:50:54,193 --> 01:51:00,193
It was praised for its portrayal of the life of Gandhi, the Indian independence
movement, and the deleterious results of British colonisation on India.

19
01:57:03,870 --> 01:57:09,870
It was considered to have maintained a reasonable level of historical accuracy, although many separate events were amalgamated, such
as historical meetings with individual people being combined into single fictionalized scenes for narrative pacing.

20
02:03:13,548 --> 02:03:19,548
Several events were exaggerated or invented, such as being beaten
by police while burning registration certificates.

21
02:09:23,225 --> 02:09:29,225
The chronology of Gandhi's early activism was altered, and certain historical
figures (such as Christian missionary and independence activist C.F.

22
02:15:32,903 --> 02:15:38,903
Andrews and founder of Pakistan Mohammad Ali Jinnah) were
considered to have been portrayed inaccurately.

23
02:21:42,580 --> 02:21:48,580
The film was praised for conveying Gandhi's core principles of nonviolence and human dignity
effectively, providing an accessible introduction to his life and message.

24
02:27:52,258 --> 02:27:58,258
Its production values, costume design, and Kingsley's
performance received worldwide critical acclaim.

25
02:34:01,935 --> 02:34:07,935
It became a commercial success, grossing $127.8 million on a $22 million budget.

26
02:40:11,612 --> 02:40:17,612
It received a leading eleven nominations at the 55th Academy Awards, winning eight,
including Best Picture, Best Director, and Best Actor (for Kingsley).

27
02:46:21,290 --> 02:46:27,290
The British Film Institute ranked it as the 34th
greatest British film of the 20th century.

28
02:52:30,967 --> 02:52:36,967
The American Film Institute ranked the film 29th on
its list of most inspiring movies.

29
02:58:40,645 --> 02:58:46,645
The film explores themes of muslim, strike, prayer, freedom, independence.

30
03:04:50,322 --> 03:04:56,322
The tone is dark and emotional.
